<title>UK: No need for utility price rises - UK's Brown.</title>
<headline>No need for utility price rises - UK's Brown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>There is no need for increases in prices by British utility firms after the budget announcement of a 5.2 billion stg windfall levy on the sector, Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said.</p>
<p>&quot;I've concluded there's no need for price rises. It shouldn't happen. these utilities have had very substantial surpluses. they've made excess profits over a period of time,&quot; he said on GMTV.</p>
<p>--Cheryl Juckes +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
